From: Erfan Abdi <erfangplus@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Separate translator controls from initial and explicit guest environments

Select the authoritative environment before sizing guest stacks; preserve exact child
environments, and keep translator controls on the host side. Outside apklayer,
retain existing loader behavior.

diff --git a/base/include/berberis/base/host_environment.h b/base/include/berberis/base/host_environment.h
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/base/include/berberis/base/host_environment.h
@@ -0,0 +1,11 @@
+// apklayer patch: translator controls belong to the host, never the app environment.
+#ifndef BERBERIS_BASE_HOST_ENVIRONMENT_H_
+#define BERBERIS_BASE_HOST_ENVIRONMENT_H_
+#include <cstdlib>
+extern "C" const char* libc_bio_host_getenv(const char*) __attribute__((weak));
+namespace berberis {
+inline const char* HostGetenv(const char* name) {
+  return libc_bio_host_getenv ? libc_bio_host_getenv(name) : std::getenv(name);
+}
+}
+#endif
